**Verdict:** revise — trust intact, value high, delight clear_hit. **Blockers: 0, concerns: 5.**

**Strongest hit (UNFAMILIAR-H1/H2):** The car-keys cold open plus the thesis line "He will tell you, without flinching, that it was not his." A reader with zero football or Enneagram knowledge is oriented in ~250 words and can restate both the type answer and the borrowed-discipline thesis after one pass — the strongest possible comprehension result for this perspective.

**Highest-priority concern (UNFAMILIAR-R1):** The No. 87 section — the passage a new reader is most likely to retell — states the jersey-number origin as settled fact ("has nothing to do with luck or the draft… The number on his back is a receipt") while the evidence packet records Jason Kelce publicly calling that story retroactive myth on their own podcast in Nov 2025. The natural follow-up Google this article invites surfaces that clip and retroactively poisons trust. The repair is cheap and thesis-strengthening: frame it as Travis's own telling with Jason's dispute acknowledged — a Seven retrofitting redemptive meaning onto his number is better Type 7 evidence than the fairy-tale version.

Also notable: my one orientation search confirmed the bare-"Jones" confusion is a draft omission (Butch Jones was the newly arrived head coach who issued the suspension — the draft never says so), and the "At 36" framing is contradicted by the article's own 2024 quote dates.

